WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.980
<b>Nanbaka</b>

00:00:04.980 --> 00:00:08.860
<b>1</b>

00:00:27.520 --> 00:00:28.800
Whoa...

00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:31.210
They're even creepier up close.

00:00:31.910 --> 00:00:33.960
So is it disabled now?

00:00:33.960 --> 00:00:36.720
Their bodies are designed
much like a human's.

00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:38.800
If you go for the neck or heart,

00:00:38.800 --> 00:00:41.240
they'll cease to function for a while.

00:00:41.240 --> 00:00:42.930
Whoa, hold up!

00:00:42.930 --> 00:00:45.690
No one told me these creepy things were here!

00:00:45.950 --> 00:00:48.940
If we had, you would've freaked out.

00:00:49.360 --> 00:00:52.780
And there are more of these
underground, right?

00:00:52.780 --> 00:00:54.700
And we need to take out all of them?

00:00:54.940 --> 00:00:59.200
No, we should avoid expending too 
much energy to get through here.

00:00:59.200 --> 00:01:07.210
<b>Gogyousan
Underground Level
1</b>

00:00:59.420 --> 00:01:01.280
You're right.

00:01:01.280 --> 00:01:03.460
We're still on the first level down.

00:01:03.460 --> 00:01:07.210
We have to move quietly so they won't find us.

00:01:07.210 --> 00:01:10.700
But there are five levels, right?

00:01:10.700 --> 00:01:11.700
That means...

00:01:12.070 --> 00:01:13.790
Until we find Hajime...

00:01:14.230 --> 00:01:17.220
We need to search each level, right?

00:01:18.430 --> 00:01:22.500
If we... at least knew... what level... he was on...

00:01:23.200 --> 00:01:26.480
Who the hell keeps pulling on my cuticles?!

00:01:50.290 --> 00:01:55.460
<b>Nanbaka</b>

00:03:04.490 --> 00:03:08.200
<b>One's Own Freedom</b>

00:03:04.830 --> 00:03:08.100
Quit screaming! You'll draw even more of them!

00:03:08.100 --> 00:03:10.820
But they're so scary!

00:03:10.820 --> 00:03:12.830
Talk about pathetic...

00:03:15.700 --> 00:03:17.330
Look out, Honey-kun!

00:03:19.080 --> 00:03:21.370
Trois! What the hell?!

00:03:22.140 --> 00:03:26.050
You're the only hottie around who could 
look so good kissing the ground.

00:03:26.050 --> 00:03:27.480
Shut up!

00:03:29.170 --> 00:03:31.140
Hey, Jyugo! You okay?

00:03:32.360 --> 00:03:34.940
I-I-I'm perfectly okay...

00:03:35.440 --> 00:03:37.730
You look like you're already at your limit!

00:03:38.340 --> 00:03:41.610
You should train a little more.

00:03:41.920 --> 00:03:43.760
Come on! Swing those arms more!

00:03:43.760 --> 00:03:44.890
Stop that!

00:03:44.890 --> 00:03:48.000
Don't make him train at a time like this!

00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:50.000
Hey, Upa. Get down.

00:03:52.860 --> 00:03:54.080
They stopped?

00:03:54.080 --> 00:03:56.250
What's going on?

00:03:58.250 --> 00:04:00.010
<b>Management Office</b>

00:03:58.440 --> 00:04:00.060
"Management office"?

00:04:09.500 --> 00:04:12.040
Let's keep an eye on things from here for now.

00:04:12.040 --> 00:04:12.900
Yeah.

00:04:12.900 --> 00:04:15.270
What is this room, anyway?

00:04:15.270 --> 00:04:20.780
<b>Management Office</b>

00:04:15.270 --> 00:04:20.780
I heard rumors about a forbidden 
archive room once used by Enki.

00:04:21.130 --> 00:04:23.170
This is probably it.

00:04:27.610 --> 00:04:30.790
You're not looking so good.

00:04:31.280 --> 00:04:33.750
I-It's nothing, Master.

00:04:33.750 --> 00:04:36.290
I'm just a bit tired.

00:04:36.290 --> 00:04:38.220
If you say so...

00:04:38.220 --> 00:04:40.400
Nico's in bad shape.

00:04:40.400 --> 00:04:42.530
We should let him rest a bit.

00:04:42.530 --> 00:04:45.600
I'll go look for water or something.

00:04:45.600 --> 00:04:46.800
Yeah.

00:04:50.500 --> 00:04:53.810
There's no way I can find anything in here.

00:04:54.200 --> 00:04:57.890
Inmates, prisons around 
the world, and other stuff...

00:04:58.330 --> 00:05:03.300
Was the former supervisor here 
just really into his job?

00:05:05.600 --> 00:05:07.320
What is this?

00:05:10.130 --> 00:05:12.830
This is all papers, too...

00:05:13.360 --> 00:05:15.850
Most of it is data on violent criminals.

00:05:15.850 --> 00:05:19.720
Convicts, death row inmates, 
and even escapees...

00:05:19.720 --> 00:05:21.090
And this is...

00:05:24.620 --> 00:05:26.090
Hakkai...

00:05:26.960 --> 00:05:28.140
Yes?

00:05:28.770 --> 00:05:31.590
Is it true that one of the guys

00:05:31.590 --> 00:05:34.600
caught along with Sugoroku was <i>that</i> inmate?

00:05:35.130 --> 00:05:36.100
It's true.

00:05:36.310 --> 00:05:38.600
Well, that certainly was lucky.

00:05:38.600 --> 00:05:41.360
That saves us the trouble of looking for him.

00:05:56.390 --> 00:05:57.620
Who are you?

00:06:03.450 --> 00:06:05.750
You're not human, are you?

00:06:10.600 --> 00:06:14.140
If that inmate is the one from back then...

00:06:14.620 --> 00:06:20.080
I'll finish off that monster myself.

00:06:18.640 --> 00:06:21.150
<b>Confidential
Human Experimentation</b>

00:06:18.640 --> 00:06:21.150
<b>Age: 16
Gender: Male
Height: 169 cm</b>

00:06:21.150 --> 00:06:24.650
<b>Confidential
Human Experimentation</b>

00:06:21.340 --> 00:06:23.860
Human experimentation?

00:06:27.420 --> 00:06:29.920
Specimen Number 15.

00:06:30.760 --> 00:06:33.800
<i>So... that wasn't a dream?</i>

00:06:34.490 --> 00:06:35.560
Hey, Jyugo.

00:06:36.020 --> 00:06:37.790
Did you find anything over there?

00:06:39.340 --> 00:06:41.660
N-No, nothing.

00:06:41.660 --> 00:06:42.790
Oh, okay.

00:06:45.530 --> 00:06:48.330
It looks like the coast is clear.

00:06:48.330 --> 00:06:51.430
Then shouldn't we get going?

00:06:51.640 --> 00:06:52.930
Yeah.

00:06:54.720 --> 00:06:56.030
Nico, can you make it?

00:06:56.030 --> 00:06:58.430
Sorry, but there's nothing here.

00:06:58.780 --> 00:07:02.270
Yeah, I rested a little, so I'm okay.

00:07:02.270 --> 00:07:03.940
Thank you too, Jyugo-kun.

00:07:04.120 --> 00:07:05.940
Y-Yeah...

00:07:06.180 --> 00:07:07.290
Okay, let's roll.

00:07:07.290 --> 00:07:08.190
Right...

00:07:13.800 --> 00:07:15.960
<i>I don't know anything about myself,</i>

00:07:15.960 --> 00:07:19.240
<i>but everyone else knows about me.</i>

00:07:20.190 --> 00:07:22.460
<i>Elf and even the former supervisor here...</i>

00:07:27.500 --> 00:07:29.110
<i>Am I human,</i>

00:07:30.040 --> 00:07:31.430
<i>or not?</i>

00:07:35.320 --> 00:07:38.400
<i>What do I remember about myself,</i>

00:07:38.400 --> 00:07:40.200
<i>and what have I forgotten?</i>

00:07:40.200 --> 00:07:42.570
Those stairs go to the 
second underground level.

00:07:43.940 --> 00:07:47.450
As I thought, security is 
lax compared to the exit.

00:07:47.450 --> 00:07:48.480
We're in luck.

00:07:48.930 --> 00:07:50.370
Don't let your guard down.

00:07:50.370 --> 00:07:52.310
We don't know what lies ahead.

00:07:52.310 --> 00:07:53.240
Stay alert—

00:07:56.660 --> 00:07:58.550
Wh-What the hell?!

00:08:11.750 --> 00:08:13.050
Rokuriki-san...

00:08:13.340 --> 00:08:14.780
That talisman...

00:08:14.780 --> 00:08:16.050
It's the attack charm.

00:08:16.320 --> 00:08:18.100
Attack... charm?

00:08:18.100 --> 00:08:22.300
The attack charm is a 
forbidden charm that fuels

00:08:22.300 --> 00:08:24.940
the subject's combative spirit 
and forces the body to move.

00:08:25.810 --> 00:08:27.840
Unless the manipulator orders otherwise,

00:08:27.840 --> 00:08:31.570
the subject considers everything that
moves an enemy to be eliminated.

00:08:31.810 --> 00:08:34.280
The manipulator is most likely Enki.

00:08:34.280 --> 00:08:37.340
But I didn't expect him to use it on a guard.

00:08:51.560 --> 00:08:55.130
Hey, he's not avoiding 
those attacks worth shit!

00:08:55.480 --> 00:08:58.010
What are those oddly-shaped weapons?

00:08:58.010 --> 00:08:59.140
Deer hook swords.

00:08:59.970 --> 00:09:01.310
As the name says,

00:09:01.310 --> 00:09:05.240
you can use the multiple hooks, 
which resemble a deer's antlers,

00:09:05.240 --> 00:09:06.780
to snag and rip an opponent apart.

00:09:06.780 --> 00:09:09.770
Damn! I can't even see 
how his weapon's moving!

00:09:10.170 --> 00:09:11.150
However...

00:09:23.530 --> 00:09:24.600
Upa...

00:09:24.600 --> 00:09:27.170
You were so pitiful,
I couldn't bear to watch.

00:09:27.560 --> 00:09:30.160
There's nothing more pathetic 
than a martial artist

00:09:30.160 --> 00:09:32.250
who can't assess a situation.

00:09:32.760 --> 00:09:34.880
He may be Rokuriki-san,

00:09:34.880 --> 00:09:36.550
but he's being controlled now.

00:09:37.080 --> 00:09:40.040
Letting your emotions take over won't fix that.

00:09:40.040 --> 00:09:42.510
You need to be more serious.

00:09:42.510 --> 00:09:43.860
You're right.

00:09:44.810 --> 00:09:46.060
Jyugo.

00:09:46.380 --> 00:09:48.350
Please open the lock on the entrance.

00:09:48.800 --> 00:09:49.810
Sure.

00:09:53.040 --> 00:09:54.680
We're from Building 5,

00:09:54.680 --> 00:09:57.820
so we'll take care of Rokuriki-san.

00:09:58.100 --> 00:10:00.360
You guys go on ahead.

00:10:01.450 --> 00:10:02.330
But...

00:10:02.560 --> 00:10:04.830
Master, you're not coming with us?

00:10:05.110 --> 00:10:08.020
We'll catch up as soon as 
we take care of things here.

00:10:08.020 --> 00:10:12.830
Besides, it's sure to go much faster 
if only Liang and I fight.

00:10:12.830 --> 00:10:16.760
Your jailbreaking and cheating
won't be of any use here.

00:10:16.760 --> 00:10:18.720
You don't mince words, do you?!

00:10:18.720 --> 00:10:21.040
You'd better catch up soon!

00:10:21.040 --> 00:10:23.720
I can't stand scary things like those!

00:10:23.720 --> 00:10:25.200
I hate to admit it,

00:10:25.200 --> 00:10:27.210
but I feel less secure without you guys here!

00:10:27.210 --> 00:10:28.940
I'm the hot guy in this group, after all!

00:10:28.940 --> 00:10:31.240
Yeah, me too!

00:10:32.400 --> 00:10:35.730
<i>For some reason, I don't
want to be part of that.</i>

00:10:35.730 --> 00:10:37.610
Just go already!

00:10:37.870 --> 00:10:39.170
I guess we have to...

00:10:39.170 --> 00:10:41.070
Come as soon as you can, will ya?

00:10:44.280 --> 00:10:45.240
Hey!

00:10:45.240 --> 00:10:47.250
Why are you closing the door?!

00:10:47.470 --> 00:10:50.120
You guys can't unlock it, right?!

00:10:50.120 --> 00:10:51.500
Hey, Jyugo.

00:10:51.710 --> 00:10:52.630
Don't open it!

00:10:54.170 --> 00:10:55.950
Just leave it.

00:10:55.950 --> 00:10:57.260
What are you saying?

00:10:57.720 --> 00:10:58.920
I'll open it now.

00:10:58.920 --> 00:11:03.010
Jyugo, those cuffs you removed from 
us earlier are special and dangerous.

00:11:03.650 --> 00:11:08.290
They're designed to blow our limbs off 
if we try to remove them by force.

00:11:09.110 --> 00:11:11.330
Even Samon-san and the other supervisors

00:11:11.330 --> 00:11:14.770
won't be able to move if they're 
restrained by those cuffs.

00:11:14.950 --> 00:11:17.480
But you can remove them.

00:11:17.480 --> 00:11:19.560
You can unlock the cells, too.

00:11:20.600 --> 00:11:22.960
As long as you keep going,

00:11:22.960 --> 00:11:26.660
we can save the supervisors 
without being discovered by Enki.

00:11:26.910 --> 00:11:31.000
But... it'd be better if you guys go, not me.

00:11:31.800 --> 00:11:33.920
It has to be you.

00:11:34.210 --> 00:11:35.920
Please, Jyugo.

00:11:44.730 --> 00:11:45.620
Watch out!

00:11:50.930 --> 00:11:55.940
<b>Nanbaka</b>

00:11:55.940 --> 00:12:00.940
<b>Nanbaka</b>

00:12:05.820 --> 00:12:07.120
Why?

00:12:07.120 --> 00:12:08.620
We don't have time to waste.

00:12:08.620 --> 00:12:11.020
Let's just keep moving for now.

00:12:15.000 --> 00:12:22.420
To entrust such a task to someone from 
another building is very unlike you.

00:12:22.620 --> 00:12:25.930
He told me a lot about him.

00:12:25.930 --> 00:12:29.810
<b>Game Room</b>

00:12:27.710 --> 00:12:28.960
Hey, Rock.

00:12:28.960 --> 00:12:29.810
Yeah?

00:12:30.280 --> 00:12:32.680
What kind of person is Jyugo?

00:12:32.910 --> 00:12:35.690
Jyugo? Why do you ask?

00:12:36.080 --> 00:12:39.900
Well, he doesn't look like a criminal,

00:12:39.900 --> 00:12:43.700
and I don't really understand his character.

00:12:44.280 --> 00:12:46.700
I agree with you there. Everyone says that.

00:12:47.080 --> 00:12:50.700
Why was he sent here in the first place?

00:12:50.990 --> 00:12:52.610
Jailbreaking, of course.

00:12:52.610 --> 00:12:55.060
He can't do anything besides that.

00:12:55.060 --> 00:12:56.710
Can't do anything?

00:12:56.930 --> 00:13:00.420
For example, he can't add numbers any 
higher than he can count on his fingers.

00:13:00.420 --> 00:13:02.340
He adds on a kindergarten level?

00:13:02.740 --> 00:13:06.000
After breaking out, he's walked 
out and fallen into a ditch,

00:13:06.000 --> 00:13:07.940
been forced to buy a weird pot,

00:13:07.940 --> 00:13:10.300
gotten mugged by a grade schooler,

00:13:10.300 --> 00:13:14.710
been snagged by an old palm reader, 
and all kinds of other stuff.

00:13:14.710 --> 00:13:16.730
He sounds more like a victim.

00:13:16.970 --> 00:13:19.920
And he runs out of steam fast,
which makes things dicey.

00:13:19.920 --> 00:13:22.480
Rock always has to carry 
him when we run away.

00:13:22.730 --> 00:13:25.180
Jyugo-kun can't swim.

00:13:25.180 --> 00:13:27.370
He'd even drown in the bath,

00:13:27.370 --> 00:13:30.070
if we didn't hold him up every evening.

00:13:31.000 --> 00:13:33.610
In short, he lacks knowledge, 
common sense, and strength.

00:13:33.610 --> 00:13:34.680
He's got nothing.

00:13:34.680 --> 00:13:36.750
That's the kind of guy Jyugo is.

00:13:36.750 --> 00:13:39.430
He really can't do anything.

00:13:39.430 --> 00:13:40.500
Yep, yep.

00:13:40.760 --> 00:13:42.720
I can hear you, assholes!

00:13:42.720 --> 00:13:44.290
But it's the truth.

00:13:44.290 --> 00:13:45.260
Yeah!

00:13:46.330 --> 00:13:48.260
I still don't understand him.

00:13:48.520 --> 00:13:51.760
Jyugo is fine the way he is.

00:13:52.280 --> 00:13:55.640
He gave me freedom that day.

00:13:56.040 --> 00:13:58.620
He pulled me out of a lousy life.

00:13:59.720 --> 00:14:04.190
So I want to do everything I can for Jyugo.

00:14:04.190 --> 00:14:07.220
Don't you have someone like that?

00:14:07.220 --> 00:14:10.610
<i>At the time, I thought Rock's "freedom"</i>

00:14:10.610 --> 00:14:15.910
<i>simply meant his sense of liberation 
when he got out of prison.</i>

00:14:16.520 --> 00:14:19.580
<i>But I was wrong.</i>

00:14:21.120 --> 00:14:28.680
<i>The reason I train every day, 
even though I'm a criminal,</i>

00:14:29.250 --> 00:14:33.940
<i>is because I want to repay the 
man I consider my mentor.</i>

00:14:38.890 --> 00:14:40.190
<i>And yet...</i>

00:14:43.690 --> 00:14:45.690
<i>I couldn't get to him.</i>

00:14:46.280 --> 00:14:49.320
<i>I was so powerless, I only dragged him down.</i>

00:14:50.920 --> 00:14:55.450
<i>What can I do at this point?</i>

00:14:57.930 --> 00:15:00.710
<i>No, I can't do anything.</i>

00:15:01.960 --> 00:15:04.130
<i>I was confident in my strength.</i>

00:15:04.130 --> 00:15:06.310
<i>I was confident in my techniques.</i>

00:15:06.310 --> 00:15:11.110
<i>But they were all neutralized so easily.</i>

00:15:11.650 --> 00:15:16.860
<i>I can't protect myself or help others.</i>

00:15:22.440 --> 00:15:23.680
<i>Freedom...</i>

00:15:24.230 --> 00:15:29.350
<i>What I'd wished for, but had given up on, 
was suddenly right in front of me.</i>

00:15:30.520 --> 00:15:32.750
<i>The "freedom" Rock spoke of...</i>

00:15:32.750 --> 00:15:35.120
<i>I finally understand it now.</i>

00:15:36.480 --> 00:15:38.500
My freedom is...

00:15:38.940 --> 00:15:42.000
the fact that even I can do something.

00:15:42.520 --> 00:15:44.520
Jyugo gave me that chance.

00:15:44.520 --> 00:15:46.970
For that, I thank him from 
the bottom of my heart.

00:15:48.010 --> 00:15:52.380
Well, if you're that certain, 
I have no choice but to trust you.

00:15:52.900 --> 00:15:56.890
In any case, it was appropriate 
to let them move ahead.

00:15:57.110 --> 00:16:01.320
Aw, man. I thought I'd have 
a chance to kill you all,

00:16:01.320 --> 00:16:03.620
but you let them get away.

00:16:03.620 --> 00:16:06.900
I didn't expect him to be out, too.

00:16:06.900 --> 00:16:10.900
Oh, well. I'll just go after them.

00:16:11.180 --> 00:16:12.840
You're not going anywhere.

00:16:12.840 --> 00:16:15.910
We're going to fight you here.

00:16:17.230 --> 00:16:22.410
Since when did you become so 
insolent to your former boss?

00:16:22.640 --> 00:16:25.420
Hachiman, why are you here?

00:16:25.420 --> 00:16:28.870
Huh? Because I escaped, obviously.

00:16:28.870 --> 00:16:30.420
Are you stupid?

00:16:31.100 --> 00:16:33.430
You smell as disgusting as ever.

00:16:33.430 --> 00:16:39.930
They let me out on the condition that 
I patrol the underground a bit.

00:16:39.930 --> 00:16:43.520
And "patrol" means that 
if I find people like you,

00:16:43.520 --> 00:16:46.190
I can get rid of them, right?

00:16:46.440 --> 00:16:49.440
I never forgot about you traitors.

00:16:49.440 --> 00:16:52.940
I've been itching to kill the two of you!

00:16:56.470 --> 00:16:57.850
He's coming.

00:16:57.850 --> 00:16:58.700
Yes.

00:17:01.880 --> 00:17:05.210
<i>To grasp the hook, which moves like a wave,</i>

00:17:05.210 --> 00:17:08.210
<i>it's better to turn it aside than receive it.</i>

00:17:08.210 --> 00:17:11.460
<i>As long as he can see the 
movement of the sword...</i>

00:17:19.000 --> 00:17:20.720
You're fast.

00:17:33.160 --> 00:17:33.990
Sorry.

00:17:34.640 --> 00:17:37.890
I was taught not to hold back.

00:17:44.920 --> 00:17:47.410
You're surprisingly amazing.

00:17:47.410 --> 00:17:48.410
What do you mean?

00:17:48.410 --> 00:17:50.110
I mean your jailbreaking.

00:17:50.110 --> 00:17:53.900
You can always unlock and 
open everything that easily?

00:17:53.900 --> 00:17:55.170
I guess.

00:17:55.170 --> 00:17:58.760
I think it's amazing that you can do 
something like that so effortlessly.

00:17:59.150 --> 00:18:01.040
It's not something just anyone can do.

00:18:01.040 --> 00:18:03.610
I'm beginning to see you in a new light.

00:18:04.570 --> 00:18:05.550
Oh...

00:18:06.460 --> 00:18:09.850
I bet you've been called a wet 
blanket before, haven't you?

00:18:09.850 --> 00:18:10.520
Huh?

00:18:10.810 --> 00:18:13.850
Typically, when someone is praised,
either they feel happy

00:18:13.850 --> 00:18:16.800
or they get full of themselves,
like Honey-kun.

00:18:16.800 --> 00:18:19.280
Huh? What did you say about me?

00:18:19.580 --> 00:18:20.960
Damn you, Trois.

00:18:20.960 --> 00:18:23.120
Are you talking shit about me again?

00:18:23.120 --> 00:18:24.990
Who the hell do you think you are?

00:18:24.990 --> 00:18:27.570
See? There are amusing people like him,

00:18:27.570 --> 00:18:30.170
who get confrontational 
whether you praise them or not.

00:18:30.170 --> 00:18:32.220
Who are you talking about, huh?

00:18:34.110 --> 00:18:38.000
<i>He acts as though none of 
this is his business.</i>

00:18:38.000 --> 00:18:40.150
<i>The rumors are true. He's an odd one.</i>

00:18:41.020 --> 00:18:46.430
It's irritating when you look indifferent, 
even though I'm genuinely complimenting you.

00:18:46.430 --> 00:18:48.130
Even the guys from Building 5 trusted you

00:18:48.130 --> 00:18:51.190
with this job because they 
believe in your ability, correct?

00:18:51.420 --> 00:18:54.380
But... I'm not...

00:18:54.380 --> 00:18:58.320
Why don't you try to take a little 
more interest in other people?

00:18:58.320 --> 00:19:02.740
Maybe try to find out how people 
feel and think about you,

00:19:02.740 --> 00:19:06.190
and what you can do to make others 
feel happy and have a good time.

00:19:07.020 --> 00:19:08.140
If you do that,

00:19:08.140 --> 00:19:11.020
you'll start to understand more 
about others as well as yourself.

00:19:11.020 --> 00:19:14.210
Besides, if you stay the way you are, 
girls will never like you.

00:19:15.450 --> 00:19:18.440
Girls won't like you, huh? Poor baby!

00:19:18.440 --> 00:19:20.440
So girls don't like you, huh?

00:19:20.440 --> 00:19:22.700
I guess that means I was right.

00:19:22.700 --> 00:19:25.580
Shut up! I may not look it, 
but I have thin body hair,

00:19:25.580 --> 00:19:27.350
and my nipples are pink!

00:19:27.350 --> 00:19:29.480
That comeback brings back memories.

00:19:29.680 --> 00:19:32.430
No, no. That thinking is so immature.

00:19:32.430 --> 00:19:33.970
To be truly popular with girls,

00:19:33.970 --> 00:19:36.690
you must first improve your inner self.

00:19:37.160 --> 00:19:40.200
Though, first and foremost,
you have to be handsome.

00:19:40.200 --> 00:19:42.990
Oh, how unfortunate for you two.

00:19:42.990 --> 00:19:44.140
Shut up!

00:19:44.140 --> 00:19:46.500
There's no question that I'm
the best-looking one here!

00:19:46.500 --> 00:19:48.830
Moron! Go back to your 
past life and try again!

00:19:48.830 --> 00:19:50.610
What was that?!

00:19:50.610 --> 00:19:52.560
What do you think, Nico?

00:19:52.560 --> 00:19:55.580
Who's the best-looking guy here?

00:19:55.580 --> 00:19:56.500
Huh?

00:19:56.820 --> 00:19:59.090
What?!

00:19:59.510 --> 00:20:03.270
Aw, you were beaten so easily.

00:20:03.270 --> 00:20:05.860
So useless, jeez.

00:20:05.860 --> 00:20:10.310
The guards are all weak,
but they think they're hot shit

00:20:10.310 --> 00:20:13.020
just because we can't do anything.

00:20:13.410 --> 00:20:17.410
I didn't get out because
I hate being in prison.

00:20:17.980 --> 00:20:21.920
The roles of inmate and 
guard get in the way here,

00:20:21.920 --> 00:20:24.720
but roles don't matter outside.

00:20:24.720 --> 00:20:27.350
If you have power, you can obtain anything.

00:20:27.350 --> 00:20:28.530
Isn't that right?

00:20:28.920 --> 00:20:34.290
That's the rule of the 
underworld you guys lived in.

00:20:34.600 --> 00:20:38.410
I don't care if that little monkey guard 
is mentoring you guys or whatever,

00:20:38.410 --> 00:20:41.270
but there's no way you two 
can be decent human beings

00:20:41.270 --> 00:20:45.310
after the training you
endured in the underworld.

00:20:46.050 --> 00:20:48.430
I told you before, didn't I?

00:20:48.430 --> 00:20:49.830
People are trash.

00:20:49.830 --> 00:20:52.060
They're perishable goods
that supply an income.

00:20:52.300 --> 00:20:55.090
Become strong to make the weak submit.

00:20:55.090 --> 00:20:58.060
Kill your feelings. Get rid of your emotions.

00:20:58.060 --> 00:21:01.570
<b>Explode</b>

00:20:58.060 --> 00:21:01.570
I'll teach you guys again.

00:21:01.840 --> 00:21:04.570
Your skills are simply tools of the trade.

00:21:04.570 --> 00:21:08.210
Don't you dare impose your sense of 
justice on me when you're only my tool.

00:21:08.210 --> 00:21:09.640
It's revolting!

00:21:12.050 --> 00:21:16.210
Your breath stinks, you damn pig!

00:21:19.700 --> 00:21:23.630
You're right. We don't know anything 
about joining society.

00:21:23.630 --> 00:21:28.270
That's why we want to learn 
here and start fresh.

00:21:28.270 --> 00:21:29.890
We want to gain a lot of knowledge.

00:21:30.390 --> 00:21:33.390
By the way, what was it 
that you said earlier?

00:21:33.390 --> 00:21:36.750
When, exactly, did we become your tools?

00:21:36.750 --> 00:21:39.400
Don't act like you own us, you pig!

00:21:39.690 --> 00:21:42.530
If you want to go back to the 
world where power is everything,

00:21:42.530 --> 00:21:43.900
then by all means, go.

00:21:44.510 --> 00:21:49.190
But you'll have to beat me first.

00:23:24.960 --> 00:23:39.980
<b>Next Episode</b>

00:23:25.700 --> 00:23:29.700
The man in the pig mask who 
appeared in front of us, Hachiman...

00:23:29.700 --> 00:23:33.120
He's the former boss of Master and Liang-kun.

00:23:33.590 --> 00:23:35.220
And I...

00:23:35.220 --> 00:23:36.100
I...

00:23:36.510 --> 00:23:39.980
<b>A Fool</b>

00:23:36.690 --> 00:23:38.670
Next episode: "A Fool."
